RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
January 24, 2011
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date
beginning at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen;
COUNCIL MEMBERS - Mr. Allen, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Mr. Collins, Dr. Rinne, Mr.
Pierson, Mr. Spiker and Mr. Valdez.  Absent: Ms. Ash.  Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City
Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Dan White, City Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was
recited.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and
support by two other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be
considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.)  Mr. Brown moved to approve Consent
Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Pierson.  Motion carried. Voting “yes” – all members of the
governing body present.
[CA]
Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on January 10, 2011.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
[CA]
Minutes from Vouchers Meeting of the Governing Body on January 18, 2011.  Motion
(per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Valdez moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Spiker.  Mr. Brown declared a conflict of interest (business interest) due to a voucher payable to
Ameri-Tech HVAC Services, and vacated Council Chambers.  Motion carried. Voting “yes” –
all members of the governing body present in Council Chambers.  Following announcement of
the vote, Mr. Brown returned to Council Chambers.
“An Ordinance amending Section 2.04.060, Meetings of the Governing Body, of Chapter
2.04, Mayor and City Council, of Title 2, Administration and Personnel, of the City of Cheyenne
Code.” Reporting for Finance Committee, Mr. Valdez moved to approve on third and final
reading, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Upon inquiry, City Treasurer Barb Dorr advised her
department has not received any phone calls or inquiries from the public or vendors regarding
the ordinance, which will change the voucher approval/payment schedule.  Motion carried.
Voting “yes” –  all members of the governing body present. (#3912)
An Ordinance amending Section 9.16.100 (B),  Open House Assembly, of Chapter 9.16,
Offenses By or Against Minors, of Title 9, Public Peace and Welfare, of the Code of the City of
Cheyenne, Wyoming, pertaining to the definition of ‘Adult’ -- referred to Public Services
Committee (sponsor - Ms. Broyles).
