### Page 2 of 6

```text
“A Resolution designating the Sundays during 2011 that annual liquor licensees may
extend dispensing room hours of operation for sales until 2:00 a.m. the following day.”  Bryan
Grzegorczyk, President, Laramie County Liquor Dealers Association, spoke in favor of the
resolution and provided information about the Association; community programs supported by
Association members through fund-raising efforts, and the Association’s support of the Police
Department’s D.U.I. and Underage Drinking Task Force. He noted that local bar owners have
purchased approximately1,500 taxi rides for its patrons to assist with responsible and safe
driving.  Jon Coverdale, Crown Bar, also spoke in favor of the resolution.  Reporting for Finance
Committee, Mr. Valdez stated there was no recommendation on the item from the Committee.
Mr. Valdez moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Upon inquiry regarding past approval of
similar resolutions, City Clerk Carol Intlekofer advised that, to the best of her recollection,
resolutions for the four Sundays had been approved annually since the mid-1980s, with the
possible exception of date changes.  Discussion followed and included state statute wording
providing that the licensing authority “may” (not “shall”) approve the four Sundays request, and
that approval of the extended hours would add approximately 16 additional hours of operation
during 2011 that licensees could, if they chose to do so, remain open on the four Sundays until
2:00 a.m. the following day.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body
present with the exception of Ms. Broyles, Mr. Pierson and Mr. Spiker voting “no”.  (#5255)
“A Resolution authorizing the Mayor and the City Clerk to sign a Final Plat for Norris
