### Page 3 of 6

```text
staff recommendations #1 through 3 and #5 through 7, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Upon inquiry
regarding any proposed parking restrictions the developer may place on campers, trailers, boats
and recreational vehicles, John Steil, Steil Surveying Services, agent for the developer, indicated
either by signage or covenants the parking of these types of vehicles will not be allowed.  Upon
further inquiry whether there will be a development wide covenant prohibiting parking of
recreational type vehicles, Dan Montgomery, developer, advised it is his intent to prohibit or
restrict parking of these types of vehicles in the high density residential areas.  It was clarified
that staff and the developer have agreed that a 20 ft. pedestrian easement, previously proposed as
an addition to staff recommendation #4, was not included in the staff recommendations noted in
the motion. Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
